<h1 class="govuk-heading-xl">Carbon</h1>

<p class="govuk-body-l">
  Page-type byte budgets, measured from the pages as they actually render. The
  build fails if a budget is exceeded.
</p>

<div class="govuk-inset-text">
  Directional figures for comparing design decisions, not audited emissions data.
  SWDM v4 via CO2.js, GB grid intensity, green hosting assumed false. There is
  deliberately no rating: an absolute figure is not good or bad on its own.
</div>

<h2 class="govuk-heading-m">Budgets and current measurements</h2>
<p class="govuk-body-s">
  Budgets from <code>carbon-budgets.json</code>, measurements from the committed
  baseline. Both are the files the check itself reads.
</p>

<table class="govuk-table govuk-body-s">
  <thead class="govuk-table__head">
    <tr class="govuk-table__row">
      <th scope="col" class="govuk-table__header">Page type</th>
      <th scope="col" class="govuk-table__header">HTML</th>
      <th scope="col" class="govuk-table__header">JavaScript</th>
      <th scope="col" class="govuk-table__header">Fonts</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody class="govuk-table__body">
    {% for p in system.pages %}
    <tr class="govuk-table__row">
      <th scope="row" class="govuk-table__header">{{ p.name | title }}</th>
      <td class="govuk-table__cell">
        {% if p.measured %}{{ p.measured.html | bytes }} / {% endif %}{{ p.budget.html | bytes }}
      </td>
      <td class="govuk-table__cell">
        {% if p.measured %}{{ p.measured.js | bytes }} / {% endif %}{{ p.budget.js | bytes }}
      </td>
      <td class="govuk-table__cell">{{ p.budget.fonts | bytes }}</td>
    </tr>
    {% endfor %}
  </tbody>
</table>

<p class="govuk-body-s">
  Shared stylesheet: {{ system.baseline.css | bytes }} gzipped, against a
  {{ system.budgets['question-page'].css | bytes }} budget.
</p>

<h2 class="govuk-heading-m">Why the fonts budget is zero</h2>
<p class="govuk-body">
  Outside the GOV.UK proposition a service must not use GDS Transport, so Defra
  mode uses a system font stack. That removes two font files rather than making
  them smaller — around 63 KB on a first uncached load, which is the largest
  single saving here and more than every other decision put together. The budget
  is zero rather than merely small because there is nothing left to download.
</p>

<h2 class="govuk-heading-m">What the number is not</h2>
<p class="govuk-body">
  It is not a score, and nothing here is graded. The uncertainty in the model
  cannot support a grade, and a grade travels out of context in a way a raw
  number does not. Compare against the committed baseline, or against the
  alternative design decision, and publish the method alongside any figure.
</p>
<p class="govuk-body">
  Green hosting is the largest lever and is not in this repository: it sits with
  Core Delivery Platform. Report that alongside any figure taken from here.
</p>
